<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stocks mixed.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			20/3/97		  13/3/97	     22/3/96</p>
<p>    Gasoline	550-575			550		   700</p>
<p>    Naphtha	     100			100		75-100</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,700-1,750		    1,750		 1,900</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	325-350		  300-325		   400</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		 10-20</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks rose slightly with rapid throughput of incoming cargoes and departing barges.</p>
<p>Naphtha stocks were broadly balanced.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks dipped with some coverage of short-term obligations. Market set to adapt to summer specification material from April 1 which should add to inventories shortly.</p>
<p>Fuel oil stocks rose slightly as product arrived, but the ARA bunker market absorbed little. Some straight-run product went to Germany.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks barely changed.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
